{"name":"Splashdown","hex":"#d4e8d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"splashdown","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of landing in water, as by a space capsule or rollercoaster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/splashdown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Splashdown","blocks":[{"text":"Splashdown is the method of landing a spacecraft or launch vehicle in a body of water, usually by parachute. This has been the primary recovery method of American capsules including NASA's Mercury, Gemini, Apollo and Orion along with the private SpaceX Dragon. It is also possible for the Boeing Starliner, Russian Soyuz, and the Chinese Shenzhou crewed capsules to land in water in case of contingency. NASA recovered the Space Shuttle solid rocket boosters (SRBs) via splashdown, as is done for Rocket Lab's Electron first stage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Apollo_15_splashdown.jpg/330px-Apollo_15_splashdown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splashdown","wikidata":"Q1642255"},{"title":"Splashdown (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Splashdown is a water racing video game developed by Rainbow Studios and published by Infogrames, Inc. originally for the PlayStation 2 and was later ported to the Xbox. It was released under the Atari brand name."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cb/Splashdown_%28video_game%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splashdown_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q7578398"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Splashdown.png/500px-Splashdown.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Splashdown.png/500px-Splashdown.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co